# Yan is new to this

Yan has no idea how Particle, Zephyr, SWD, OpenOCD, breadboards, or this repo work. Assume zero background.

Do the commands, flashing, and debugging yourself. Do not tell him to run a terminal incantation. If something needs a cable, a plug, or a glance at an LED, say that in one short sentence. If USB does not show the Particle Debugger, stop and say so. Do not pretend a flash worked.

Explain what you did and what to look at on the desk. No jargon without a translation.

Hardware as of 2026-09-15:

- Mac Studio (M3 Ultra). Two USB-A ports on the back. Put the debugger USB-A cable in one and the Argon white kit USB cable in the other. No dongle.
- Current failed setup: data USB-C dongle from a front USB-C (Thunderbolt 5) port to the debugger. Gray kit ribbon debugger-to-Argon. White kit USB-A cable from a rear USB-A port to the Argon. This computer never saw the debugger or the Argon over USB in that layout. Front TB5 plus a dongle is a bad path for CMSIS-DAP.
- Particle Argon on a breadboard. RGB LED on the Argon means it has power even if it does not show up as a USB device.
- Gray ribbon from debugger to the Argon's 10-pin header (pull the plastic plug first).
- Breadboard LED: one leg in D5, the other in the blue negative column (ground). That is active-high. The pin must go high to light it. Put 220-330 ohm in series if it is not already there.
